# Crusader of Light

## Lore

The Crusaders of Light are the warrior order of the Adraodan Minotaurs, a tribe that spent seventy thousand years underground atoning for its ancestors'' service to the Old Ones. They are knights in most respects: trained from youth in arms, discipline, courtesy and letters, and sworn to protect the weak and oppose evil wherever it is found. Nearly a third of the tribe follows this calling.

What sets a Crusader apart from any other knight is the mind. Every Adraodan is psychic, and the Crusader''s training turns that gift toward the battlefield and the vigil. In place of horsemanship, the lance and the study of heraldry, the Crusader masters seven psionic powers of awareness and of the body.

The order has only just stepped into the daylight. Its members have never even heard of humans, and they intend to set the standard for heroes all the same.

## Alignment

The class prints no alignment line of its own. The race''s line, printed 142: any; most good or unprincipled, rarely anarchist or evil.

## GM Notes

Treat a Crusader as a Knight for every rule this entry does not change, including the code a knight is expected to live by. The book''s one named Crusader is Nekaradon, the tribe''s leader: principled, 3rd level.

The class teaches no horsemanship.
